{
  "Introduction to Choice in a World of Scarcity": "导论：稀缺世界中的选择",
  "Choices and Tradeoffs ": "选择与权衡",
  "Choices ... to What Degree?": "选择……读到什么学位？",
  "Does your level of education impact earning? Let’s look at some data from the Bureau of Labor Statistics (BLS). In 2020, among full-time wage and salary workers, median weekly earnings for those with a master’s degree were $1,545. Multiply this average by 52 weeks, and you get average annual earnings of $80,340. Compare that to the median weekly earnings for full-time workers aged 25 and over with just a bachelor’s degree: $1,305 weekly and $67,860 a year. What about those with no higher than a high school diploma in 2020? They earn an average of just $781 weekly and $40,612 over 12 months. In other words, data from the BLS indicates that receiving a bachelor’s degree boosts earnings by 67% over what workers would have earned if they only obtained a high school diploma, and a master’s degree yields average earnings that are nearly double those of workers with a high school diploma.": "受教育程度会影响收入吗？我们来看美国劳工统计局（BLS）的一些数据。2020 年，在全职领取工资或薪金的劳动者中，拥有硕士学位者的每周收入中位数为 1,545 美元。将这一数额乘以 52 周，折算的年收入为 80,340 美元。相比之下，25 岁及以上、仅拥有学士学位的全职劳动者，每周收入中位数为 1,305 美元，折算年收入为 67,860 美元。2020 年学历不超过高中毕业的人呢？他们每周平均收入仅为 781 美元，按 12 个月折算为 40,612 美元。换句话说，BLS 的数据表明，获得学士学位的人，其收入比只取得高中文凭时可能获得的收入高出 67%；拥有硕士学位者的平均收入，则几乎是高中毕业者的两倍。",
  "Given these statistics, we might expect many people to choose to go to college and at least earn a bachelor’s degree. Assuming that people want to improve their material well-being, it seems like they would make those choices that provide them with the greatest opportunity to consume goods and services. As it turns out, the analysis is not nearly as simple as this. In fact, in 2019, the BLS reported that while just over 90% of the population aged 25 and over in the United States had a high school diploma, only 36% of those aged 25 and over had a bachelor's or higher degree, and only 13.5% had earned a master's or higher degree.": "看到这些统计数据，我们可能会认为，许多人会选择上大学，至少取得学士学位。如果人们希望改善自己的物质生活，那么他们似乎应当选择能带来最多商品与服务消费机会的方案。然而，事情远没有这么简单。事实上，根据 BLS 在 2019 年报告的数据，美国 25 岁及以上人口中，高中毕业者的比例略超过 90%，但拥有学士或更高学位者仅占 36%，取得硕士或更高学位者仅占 13.5%。",
  "This brings us to the subject of this chapter: why people make the choices they make and how economists explain those choices.": "这就引出了本章的主题：人们为什么作出这样的选择，以及经济学家如何解释这些选择。",
  "In this chapter, you will learn about:": "本章将介绍：",
  "How Individuals Make Choices Based on Their Budget Constraint": "个人如何根据预算约束作出选择",
  "The Production Possibilities Frontier and Social Choices": "生产可能性边界与社会选择",
  "Confronting Objections to the Economic Approach": "回应对经济学分析方法的质疑",
  "The Concept of Opportunity Cost": "机会成本的概念",
  "Marginal Decision-Making and Diminishing Marginal Utility": "边际决策与边际效用递减",
  "Sunk Costs": "沉没成本",
  "Productive Efficiency and Allocative Efficiency": "生产效率与配置效率",
  "The greatest improvements in the productive powers of labour, and the greater part of the skill, dexterity, and judgment, with which it is anywhere directed, or applied, seem to have been the effects of the division of labour. The effects of the division of labour, in the general business of society, will be more easily understood, by considering in what manner it operates in some particular manufactures. It is commonly supposed to be carried furthest in some very trifling ones; not perhaps that it really is carried further in them than in others of more importance: but in those trifling manufactures which are destined to supply the small wants of but a small number of people, the whole number of workmen must necessarily be small; and those employed in every different branch of the work can often be collected into the same workhouse, and placed at once under the view of the spectator.": "劳动生产力的巨大提高，以及运用劳动时所体现的大部分技能、熟练程度和判断力，似乎都来自劳动分工。要理解分工对社会生产活动的影响，考察它在某些具体制造业中的运作方式会更容易。人们通常认为，一些规模很小的制造业将分工推进得最为彻底。这未必是说，它们的分工实际上比其他更重要的制造业更细；而是因为，这些小型制造业只需满足少数人的少量需求，工人总数必然不多，各道工序上的工人往往能够集中在同一间作坊里，让观察者一眼看清整个生产过程。",
  "In those great manufactures, on the contrary, which are destined to supply the great wants of the great body of the people, every different branch of the work employs so great a number of workmen, that it is impossible to collect them all into the same workhouse. We can seldom see more, at one time, than those employed in one single branch. Though in such manufactures, therefore, the work may really be divided into a much greater number of parts, than in those of a more trifling nature, the division is not near so obvious, and has accordingly been much less observed.": "相反，在满足广大人口大量需求的大型制造业中，每一道工序都雇用了许多工人，不可能将他们全部集中在同一间作坊里。我们一次所能看到的，往往只是某一道工序上的工人。因此，这些大型制造业中的劳动虽然实际上可能比小型制造业分成更多环节，但分工却远没有那么直观，也因此较少受到注意。"
}
